## 46. Create private data members and access them through methods. Honesty note, verified directly: plain private: is a documented convention, not an enforced boundary -- w.balance below reads successfully even though balance is marked private. Karly's real, enforced access control is priblock/problock (hash-chain sealed), used in program 055 onward wherever this list specifically calls for preventing direct access. ##
class Wallet {
    private:
        dou balance;
    public:
    fun __init__(dou b) {
        this.balance = b;
    }
    fun get_balance() -> dou {
        return this.balance;
    }
}
auto w = new Wallet(1000.0);
show("Balance via the intended method:", w.get_balance());
show("Balance via direct access anyway (not actually blocked):", w.balance);
